Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] P6.1 player name screen (Digimon Online registration) fills 16:9

The player name screen of the opening (STPLNMET: the welcome, the account
name, the starter pack and the confirmation) ran with gutter 0, 4:3. It now
takes the menu gutter (port/options/widescreen.c) and fills it:

- The backdrop's three hexagon layers are periodic (the two scrolling ones
  start over every -STPLNMET_scrollEnds[i] pixels right and half that up, the
  still one every 168 right and 84 up). DW3_WIDE_PERIODIC adds, at draw time,
  the copies of their hexagons moved by whole periods that show in a gutter.
- The welcome panel's and the confirmation bar's side lines, which run to the
  4:3 edges, run to the picture's edges: DW3_WIDE_WINGS repeats their outer
  8 columns (straight lines) across the gutters.

Panels, keyboard and text keep their positions. Off, nothing changes.

--- a/include/menus/player_name.h
+++ b/include/menus/player_name.h
@@ -37,6 +37,18 @@
 #define PLNMET_BANK (FILE_PLNMET_BANK << 16) /* the keyboard's and partners' sprites */
 #define PLNMET_SCROLL (FILE_PLNMET_SCROLL << 16)
 
+#if PORT_HOST
+#include "port_widescreen.h"
+#else
+#define DW3_WIDE_PERIODIC(sheet, frame, x, y, dx, dy) (sheet)
+#define DW3_WIDE_WINGS(sheet, frame, x) (sheet)
+#endif
+/* The still scroll layer's period (STPLNMET_updateScroll): its hexagons repeat
+   every 168 pixels right and 84 up, as the moving layers' do every
+   -STPLNMET_scrollEnds[i] right and half that up */
+#define STPLNMET_STILL_PERIOD_X 168
+#define STPLNMET_STILL_PERIOD_Y (-84)
+
 /* Two scrolling sprites (STPLNMET_createScroll), once their image is loaded */
 typedef struct NameScroll {
     TASK_HEADER(NameScroll);
